\newlabel{tab:iw}{{I}{3}{Importance-weighting decomposition (LSIF) with block bootstrap by match ($n_{\text {boot}} = 2000$, 6 blocks per year). Baseline $\mathrm {ADE}_{2019} = 4.53$\,mm; corr.\ $= \mathrm {ADE}_y - \mathrm {ADE}_{\mathrm {IW}}$. 2024 has negative excess and is excluded from the recovery column. All classifier tests give $p < 10^{-3}$ by permutation. $^{\dagger }$2022 has a small excess (0.23\,mm), so the percentage should be read with care}{table.1}{}}
